# Page composition (MUST)

How marketing `page.tsx` files are built. Prefer fewer files for static copy; extract only when justified.

## MUST — choose the right page shape

| Page kind | MUST do | MUST NOT |
|-----------|---------|----------|
| **Nav / listing stub** (thin unfinished listing or about) | Use a shared shell (e.g. `MarketingShellPage`) + shared metadata helper (includes shared `PageHero`) | Invent a one-off duplicate shell layout |
| **Static one-off content** (terms, privacy, cookies, simple legal/about with real copy) | Put article markup **inline in `page.tsx`** (metadata + `{pageName}PageSchema` + body); use shared **`PageHero`** for title/breadcrumb chrome | Create a page-only wrapper like `TermsDocument` / `PrivacyDocument` with no reuse |
| **Product / interactive UI** (home hero, contact form, cards, filters) | Keep page as Server Component; extract **reusable or client** pieces to `components/sections/<usage>/` (or `ui/`) | Wrap the whole page in `"use client"`; extract static legal prose “for thinness” alone |

## MUST — shared inner-page chrome

- Inner marketing pages (not home) use `PageHero` (or equivalent shared chrome) for breadcrumb + H1 (+ optional eyebrow/description/image).
- Hero images come from config (e.g. `PAGE_HERO_IMAGES` / path helpers in `src/config/site.ts`) — not hardcoded URLs in pages.
- Home keeps its own hero; do not put inner-page `PageHero` on the home route.

## MUST — section folders (by usage)

Group under `src/components/sections/`:

| Folder | Use for |
|--------|---------|
| `chrome/` | Shared inner-page chrome (`PageHero`, marketing shell) |
| Feature folders (e.g. `contact/`, `browse/`) | Feature-area sections when that area grows |

Add a new usage folder when a feature area grows; do not dump unrelated sections at the `sections/` root.

## MUST — when to extract a section

Extract to `src/components/sections/<usage>/` only if at least one is true:

1. **Reused** on more than one route, or clearly shared soon.
2. **Client interactivity** (`"use client"`, forms, browser APIs) — keep a small leaf.
3. **Multi-block product UI** where the route would otherwise mix several distinct interactive/composable blocks (e.g. home hero + listings).

Do **not** extract solely to “keep `page.tsx` thin” when the body is static, route-specific prose.

## MUST — page always owns SEO wiring

- Metadata via `buildPageMetadata` (or a shared shell metadata helper for stubs).
- JSON-LD as `{pageName}PageSchema()` on the page (stubs may use the helper’s built-in schema).
- Shared helpers only in `lib/schema.ts` / `lib/metadata.ts`.

## Examples

```tsx
// Stub — OK (PageHero inside shared shell)
<MarketingShellPage title={…} description={…} path={paths.about} body="…" />

// Legal / static — OK (PageHero + inline body on page.tsx)
<>
  <PageHero title={…} breadcrumbs={[…]} image={PAGE_HERO_IMAGES.terms} />
  <Container as="article">…sections of copy…</Container>
</>

// Contact when form exists — OK
<>
  <Container>…intro copy…</Container>
  <ContactForm /> {/* client leaf in sections/ */}
</>
```

```tsx
// BAD — one-off section with no reuse/interaction
// components/sections/TermsDocument.tsx used only by terms/page.tsx
```

